Final independent review log (fresh full-diff review at the final tree)
======================================================================

Reviewer: DeepSeek V4.1 Flash via the Copilot CLI BYOK route
(CommandCode), --reasoning-effort xhigh. Subscription quota remained
exhausted (HTTP 429), so the BYOK route served the review; routing is
documented in the review skill and never carries credentials into the
repository.

Scope: `git diff ef98a2d..HEAD` at HEAD b96509f (the complete goal
diff), verified against the files at HEAD with reproduction-first
triage. The reviewer also swept every secret-bearing surface (eval,
convert, doc, lock, inspect schema/path, viz, debug, explain, lint,
patch, repair, compatibility, generate, graph, LSP hover/completion/
inlay/semantic/code-action/explain/debug-steps, FFI/WASM) and found no
raw secret material; the only oracle behaviour it noted is the
documented blob hash/size identity.

Findings (7) and fixes at fcea0d3
---------------------------------
F1 HIGH    LSP `active/debug/steps` used Engine::new() (ambient env), so a
           step could show a host value hover/diagnostics report as null.
           Fixed: Engine::hermetic() + wall clock off.
           Test: step_bridge_is_hermetic_for_environment_reads.
F2 HIGH    Formatter Enum branch returned before the shared argument list,
           dropping default/description/requires (changing requiredness,
           defaults, and descriptions; `fmt --check schemas/*` failed).
           Fixed: Enum renders the same arguments as other leaves.
           Tests: enum_fields_keep_every_accepted_argument,
           every_shipped_schema_round_trips_through_the_formatter.
F3 MEDIUM  Semantic `'''` verbatim form containing a CR normalized it to LF
           (value change + non-idempotence). Fixed: CR payloads use the
           escaped `"""` path.
           Test: semantic_multiline_with_a_carriage_return_keeps_its_value.
F4 MEDIUM  Brace output was not idempotent when a table's trailing comment
           followed its last nested block (the next parse moved it inside).
           Fixed: comments are hoisted into the nested block (the fixed
           point) and empty nested tables emit `key = {}`.
           Tests: brace_trailing_note_after_a_nested_block_is_idempotent,
           brace_empty_tables_keep_inter_entry_comments_idempotent.
F5 MEDIUM  59-64-level nested expressions overflowed the 1 MiB main stack
           in unoptimized builds. Fixed: CLI and LSP run commands on a
           32 MiB worker stack; 64 levels yield E004, never a crash.
           Test: deep_expression_nesting_fails_with_e004_instead_of_overflowing.
F6 LOW     `--break budget:0` was accepted although the range is 1-100.
           Fixed: 0 matches nothing; test updated in
           budget_breakpoints_match_on_count_and_percent.
F7 LOW     L016 absolute/parent-escape branches were unreachable because
           `lint` had no parse opt-in. Fixed: `lint --allow-parent-escapes`.
           Test: lint_can_report_include_escapes_when_the_parser_allows_them.

Docs updated with the fixes: spec/budgets.md (stack requirement),
spec/linter.md and docs/lint-rules.md (lint parse flag), spec/lsp.md
(hermetic debugger bridge).

Verification (round 77b, no new findings requested)
---------------------------------------------------
Every finding re-checked at HEAD fcea0d3 against the code and the named
regression test; the reviewer also formatted all eight shipped schemas
to a copy and confirmed no `default`, `description`, `requires`,
`descriptions`, `deprecated`, or `removed_in` occurrence was lost, and
that the absolute-path L016 branch fires through the live CLI.

VERDICT: ALL FIXED - zero open findings.

Close-out documentation reviews (2026-10-26, post-round-77)
----------------------------------------------------------
After the evidence refresh at c7e4ec3, two independent reviewers re-read
the close-out files: DeepSeek V4.1 Flash (Copilot BYOK, xhigh) and Meta
Muse Spark 1.3 Contributor (local BYOK proxy, xhigh). Together they
reported 13 documentation-precision issues (9 and 3, with two overlaps),
none in product code:

- the evidence README named 1fdeaf5 as the capture tree for gates.log,
  which its own header places at 1b5ce29;
- the research-battery capture date was wrong (2026-10-22 capture,
  2026-10-23 commit, not 2026-10-24);
- two historical ci.log blocks still said "HEAD" and "in_progress" for
  runs whose final conclusions are known (cancelled/superseded);
- review-final.log was labelled as unchanged since 1b5ce29 although its
  header was corrected later (verdicts unchanged);
- the evidence README repeated "Step 6" for the agent-kit row;
- the round-73/75/76 commit attribution in review-final.log was too
  broad (round-73 fixes landed at e06df6d, the round-75 bound at
  625f22c, the round-76 sweep at f6efd0d);
- the reasoning-effort scope read differently in two files;
- an orphaned C ABI/WASM paragraph read as part of round 77;
- the external tooling-proposal path looked repo-relative;
- deterministic artifacts that reproduce byte-for-byte need a provenance
  record, because a re-run leaves no git trace.

All were fixed. conformance/evidence/REFRESH.md now records the re-run at
1fdeaf5 with a SHA-256 pin per unchanged artifact, the README gives the
true capture tree per row, ci.log records final conclusions only, and the
commit attribution and effort scope are stated once and consistently.
Neither reviewer found a contradiction in the round counts, test counts,
run verdicts, vector/tool counts, or the review verdicts themselves.

VERDICT: all documentation findings fixed.